            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic sesquiterpene dilactone from Mikania cordata.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>919-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The crude extract of Mikania cordata (1 and 3 g/kg, p.o.) and deoxymikanolide (1) (10 mg/kg, p.o.) significantly inhibited acetic acid-induced writhing in mice. Three other sesquiterpene dilactones isolated from the same plant, namely mikanolide, dihydromikanolide and scandenolide, did not show significant analgesic activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
